id: healing-hands
name: Healing Hands
uaType: magical
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
tpCost: 10
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 5
# "Target another Character within your Melee Range. That Character regains 1d10(bT) Life Points. Increase the amount
# of Life Points they regain by your Magic Modifier." Who, and what its Advancements add, asked with the roll's window
# before anything is paid (use-maneuver.mjs askHeal); rolled and given on a card (chat.mjs postHealing).
heals: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Another Character within your Melee Range regains 1d10(bT) Life Points plus your Magic Modifier. Passive: Medicine
  Skill Checks 1 higher.
text: >
  Healing Hands: You can lay your hands upon your allies, restoring their vitality in the process.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
  –TP Cost: 10
  –KP Cost: 5(T)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: Increase your Medicine Skill Checks by 1.
  –Effect: Target another Character within your Melee Range. That Character regains 1d10(bT) Life Points. Increase the
  amount of Life Points they regain by your Magic Modifier.

---

# "Increase your Medicine Skill Checks by 1" - flat, not (T).
[passive]
skill.medicine.bonus += 1;
